## [e12] readOnly routing: which H2 database did a @Transactional(readOnly = true) method actually use
| DataSource given to the TransactionManager | readOnly=true method | readOnly=false method |
|---|---|---|
| (a) AbstractRoutingDataSource (key = isCurrentTransactionReadOnly) | db=WRITER readOnlyFlag=true | db=WRITER readOnlyFlag=false |
| (b) LazyConnectionDataSourceProxy(routing DataSource) | db=READER readOnlyFlag=true | db=WRITER readOnlyFlag=false |
| (c) LazyConnectionDataSourceProxy(writer) + setReadOnlyDataSource(reader) | db=READER readOnlyFlag=true | db=WRITER readOnlyFlag=false |
